KNOWNBUG
undriven_bits_frozen1.sv
--bound 4
^\[main\.p_part\] always !main\.started \|\| main\.v\[3:0\] == main\.v_prev: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p_whole\] always !main\.started \|\| main\.w == main\.w_prev: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Bits of a net that have no driver (v[3:0], where only v[7:4] is assigned) are
filled with a time-invariant nondet(main.v) rather than being free in every
timeframe.  As a result the undriven bits keep one value for the whole trace,
and p_part is wrongly reported as PROVED.

A net with no driver at all (w) is correctly free in every cycle, so p_whole
is REFUTED.  Undriven bits of a partially driven net should behave the same
way: p_part should also be REFUTED.

See https://github.com/diffblue/hw-cbmc/issues/2251
